1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
'I seek refuge in God from the accursed
Satan; in the name of God, the Most Compassionate, the Most Merciful.'

2
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:45,440
This surah — apparently — was revealed in
Medina.

3
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:54,000
It is an oath by the war-horses that
served

4
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,905
in the defense of Islam — an oath by

5
00:01:00,905 --> 00:01:07,905
these steeds in their various states:

6
00:01:07,905 --> 00:01:14,905
as they gallop panting, as their hooves

7
00:01:14,905 --> 00:01:21,905
strike sparks from the rock, and as those

8
00:01:21,905 --> 00:01:28,235
swift chargers raid the attacking

9
00:01:28,235 --> 00:01:35,140
enemy and charge into their midst at

10
00:01:35,140 --> 00:01:42,140
dawn, raising dust on the battlefield.

11
00:01:42,140 --> 00:01:49,140
This oath refers back to the jihad of

12
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:56,140
the warriors. As for camels and beasts

13
00:01:56,140 --> 00:02:03,140
of burden, they were mentioned in Surah

14
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:10,140
al-Nahl: 'and horses, mules and donkeys,

15
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:17,045
that you may ride them' (Quran 16:8)

16
00:02:17,045 --> 00:02:24,045
— recalled there as divine blessings,

17
00:02:24,045 --> 00:02:30,760
not as objects of an oath. Likewise

18
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:37,760
of the flocks He said: 'and for you there

19
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:44,760
is beauty in them when you bring them

20
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:51,760
in and when you send them out' (Quran

21
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:58,760
16:6) — this is the beauty of herding.

22
00:03:00,740 --> 00:03:07,740
The carrying capacity belongs

23
00:03:07,740 --> 00:03:14,740
to the horse, mule and donkey,

24
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:21,740
which have a role in transport;

25
00:03:21,740 --> 00:03:27,857
but in a military charge

26
00:03:27,857 --> 00:03:34,857
only the war-horse takes part

27
00:03:34,857 --> 00:03:41,857
— not mule, donkey or ass. So

28
00:03:41,857 --> 00:03:48,857
the oath refers in truth to the

29
00:03:48,857 --> 00:03:55,857
jihad of the warriors who run

30
00:03:55,857 --> 00:04:02,739
panting on the battlefield,

31
00:04:02,739 --> 00:04:09,739
whose iron-shod hooves strike

32
00:04:09,739 --> 00:04:16,739
fire from the rock; and when

33
00:04:16,739 --> 00:04:23,739
dawn comes their assault begins,

34
00:04:23,739 --> 00:04:29,092
and the plundering of

35
00:04:29,092 --> 00:04:35,974
the disbelievers is carried

36
00:04:35,974 --> 00:04:42,974
out, raising dust and clamor

37
00:04:42,974 --> 00:04:49,974
as they charge into the enemy host

38
00:04:49,974 --> 00:04:56,601
and rout them. Although it

39
00:04:56,601 --> 00:05:03,483
was also transmitted — from

40
00:05:03,483 --> 00:05:10,483
Ibn 'Abbas, via al-Tabari and

41
00:05:10,483 --> 00:05:17,483
later al-Zamakhshari's al-Kashshaf

42
00:05:17,483 --> 00:05:22,071
— that this refers

43
00:05:22,071 --> 00:05:28,953
to the pack-camels carrying

44
00:05:28,953 --> 00:05:35,953
pilgrims' loads from Mecca to

45
00:05:35,953 --> 00:05:42,580
Arafat, then Mash'ar, then

46
00:05:42,580 --> 00:05:49,580
Mina and back, what truly befits

47
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:56,207
such an oath is the charge

48
00:05:56,207 --> 00:06:03,207
of the warriors. In the Hajj it

49
00:06:03,207 --> 00:06:10,207
is the lean camels of the deep

50
00:06:10,207 --> 00:06:17,207
ravine (fajj 'amiq) that are

51
00:06:17,207 --> 00:06:24,207
spoken of — not this running,

52
00:06:24,207 --> 00:06:31,207
speed, and striking of sparks;

53
00:06:31,207 --> 00:06:37,840
none of that belongs here.

54
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:45,671
Although in Hajj and 'Umra powerful camels
come from afar,

55
00:06:45,671 --> 00:06:52,671
what the Qur'an relates refers partly to
the lean pilgrim-camels

56
00:06:52,671 --> 00:06:57,840
and partly to the deep ravine (fajj
'amiq).

57
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:04,710
In any case, the mounts other than
pilgrim-camels — in the end, there is the deep

58
00:07:04,710 --> 00:07:10,440
ravine and the pilgrim-camel; but the one
on the battlefield is the war-horse.

59
00:07:10,540 --> 00:07:17,420
The point is that although both images
occur, what befits the matter of jihad is what took place in Medina.

60
00:07:17,780 --> 00:07:24,300
And it was jihad that was able to
establish Islam.

61
00:07:24,540 --> 00:07:31,120
'Islam is exalted and nothing is exalted
above it' — a declarative sentence delivered with the intent of a command.

62
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:38,120
This — 'that He may make it prevail over
all

63
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:44,632
religion' (Quran 9:33; also 48:28, 61:9)

64
00:07:44,632 --> 00:07:51,307
— though outwardly a report, is delivered

65
00:07:51,307 --> 00:07:58,144
with performative intent. And in the close

66
00:07:58,144 --> 00:08:04,493
of Surah al-Bayyina, that the believers

67
00:08:04,493 --> 00:08:10,679
and God-fearing are the best of people

68
00:08:10,679 --> 00:08:17,679
on earth — the best, most upright, most
learned

69
00:08:17,679 --> 00:08:23,540
civilization — He said 'they are the

70
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:30,215
best of creation' (Quran 98:7). The truly

71
00:08:30,215 --> 00:08:36,401
righteous (abrar) are not merely those

72
00:08:36,401 --> 00:08:43,401
who do good deeds; the man of birr is he
whose

73
00:08:43,401 --> 00:08:50,401
heart is open like the vast plains,
unbounded

74
00:08:50,401 --> 00:08:56,587
— who says, 'O God, forgive me and all

75
00:08:56,587 --> 00:09:03,099
believing men and women in the easts and

76
00:09:03,099 --> 00:09:09,936
wests of the earth,' and, 'It is not sweet

77
00:09:09,936 --> 00:09:16,780
for me to rest while in the farthest reach

78
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:23,780
of my rule there is an orphan, a hungry
one,

79
00:09:23,780 --> 00:09:30,780
or one in distress.' He is the man of
birr.

80
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:38,900
'Bariyya' means 'the created,' so you
Muslims are the best of creatures

81
00:09:38,900 --> 00:09:44,697
— on condition that a person struggles
against disbelief,

82
00:09:44,697 --> 00:09:50,494
colonialism and tyranny, whether by the
pen or by action.

83
00:09:50,494 --> 00:09:56,495
These declarative sentences are delivered
with performative

84
00:09:56,495 --> 00:10:03,004
intent: 'you are the best of creation.' It
addresses a universal

85
00:10:03,004 --> 00:10:08,500
principle to the listener, without preface
or command.

86
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:15,214
Without 'By the chargers panting, striking
sparks, raiding at dawn, raising therein

87
00:10:15,214 --> 00:10:20,800
a cloud of dust' (Quran 100:1-4) — without
struggle, without jihad — or with them.

88
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:26,933
If it is with these, then it becomes 'the
best of creation' — the best civilization

89
00:10:26,933 --> 00:10:30,760
is yours, the best culture is yours, the
best life is yours.

90
00:10:31,140 --> 00:10:34,280
If not, this divine promise is not
realized.

91
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:40,631
In the close of Surah al-Bayyina came
'those who believe and

92
00:10:40,631 --> 00:10:47,511
do righteous deeds — they are the best of
creation' (Quran 98:7).

93
00:10:47,511 --> 00:10:53,862
Such statements, though a promise, carry a
definite command:

94
00:10:53,862 --> 00:10:59,472
you must have the best civilization,
nation, law, and

95
00:10:59,472 --> 00:11:06,458
leader — the imam of the community whom He
has appointed — and its

96
00:11:06,458 --> 00:11:12,600
measure is the Qur'an and the Pure Ones
(the Ahl al-Bayt).

97
00:11:14,560 --> 00:11:20,700
Therefore, where the discourse is about
carrying loads, the discourse is about the horse.

98
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:28,358
Where it is about combat, the discourse is
only about the horse — the

99
00:11:28,358 --> 00:11:32,680
mule and donkey have no precise part in
it, let alone the camel.

100
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:37,944
After the oaths, God Most Holy reproaches

101
00:11:37,944 --> 00:11:41,620
this human being more than fifty times.

102
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:49,660
The praise, exaltation and honor God gives
the human being go

103
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:56,660
back to his primordial nature (fitra) — to
that universal covenant:

104
00:11:56,660 --> 00:12:03,093
'And when your Lord took from the loins of
the children

105
00:12:03,093 --> 00:12:09,877
of Adam their descendants and made them
testify concerning

106
00:12:09,877 --> 00:12:16,877
themselves: Am I not your Lord? They said:
Yes' (Quran 7:172).

107
00:12:16,877 --> 00:12:22,960
All virtue and excellence go back to that
dimension.

108
00:12:23,900 --> 00:12:28,974
And all flaws and defects go back to 'man
was created' — this

109
00:12:28,974 --> 00:12:33,800
human being made from clay/mire (lajin)
goes back to that.

110
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:42,500
He said 'he indeed fails who buries it'
(Quran 91:10):

111
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:49,391
if someone buries the divine fitra that
testified

112
00:12:49,391 --> 00:12:56,391
'Yes' at the great covenant, stops its
mouth and will

113
00:12:56,391 --> 00:13:03,141
not let it speak, then his spokesman
becomes his

114
00:13:03,141 --> 00:13:10,141
caprice and desire; he moves by conjecture
and inclination.

115
00:13:10,141 --> 00:13:16,047
Even if he outwardly denies the Origin, in

116
00:13:16,047 --> 00:13:23,047
his own conscience he affirms it and
within himself

117
00:13:23,047 --> 00:13:30,047
he is a witness — for the fitra cannot be
destroyed;

118
00:13:30,047 --> 00:13:36,940
it is alive, only intrigued against and
silenced.

119
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:43,344
It is knowing and aware; it sees, knows,
and can speak; and on the Day

120
00:13:43,344 --> 00:13:48,728
of Resurrection the human being testifies
against himself: 'witnessing

121
00:13:48,728 --> 00:13:52,960
against themselves that they disbelieved'
(Quran 9:17).

122
00:13:54,260 --> 00:14:01,260
As the limbs bear witness, so does the
fitra against

123
00:14:01,260 --> 00:14:08,026
this human — who smothered the fitra and

124
00:14:08,026 --> 00:14:15,026
let his animal nature flourish; who is
'ungrateful

125
00:14:15,026 --> 00:14:21,792
to his Lord' (Quran 100:6), 'and to that

126
00:14:21,792 --> 00:14:28,792
he is a witness' (Quran 100:7), and 'and
violent

127
00:14:28,792 --> 00:14:35,792
in his love of wealth' (Quran 100:8).
'Wealth'

128
00:14:35,792 --> 00:14:42,792
is not only property: it is rank,
position,

129
00:14:42,792 --> 00:14:49,792
leadership. Man uses all that is on the
earth

130
00:14:49,792 --> 00:14:56,792
— mineral, plant, animal, human — as
tools. As

131
00:14:56,792 --> 00:15:03,792
in Surah Al 'Imran: 'beautified for people
is

132
00:15:03,792 --> 00:15:10,792
the love of desires — of women and sons,
and heaped

133
00:15:10,792 --> 00:15:17,560
hoards of gold and silver' (Quran 3:14).

134
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:25,086
'and branded horses, and cattle and
tillage' (Quran

135
00:15:25,086 --> 00:15:30,760
3:14): 'harth' (tillage) is agriculture;
'branded

136
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:36,897
horses and cattle' are livestock; the
'heaped hoards'

137
00:15:36,897 --> 00:15:42,687
are gold, silver, precious objects and
antiquities

138
00:15:42,687 --> 00:15:48,480
— the mineral; and 'sons and women' are
the human.

139
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:56,800
The heaped hoards pertain to the mineral,
the branded horses

140
00:15:56,800 --> 00:16:03,800
and cattle to animal husbandry, tillage to
plants, and 'women

141
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:10,800
and sons' to the human. He presses all
four — human, plant, mineral,

142
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:17,270
animal — into service as tools. When this
person enters

143
00:16:17,270 --> 00:16:24,270
the Resurrection, his first witness is his
fitra: 'witnessing

144
00:16:24,270 --> 00:16:30,740
against themselves that they disbelieved'
(Quran 9:17).

145
00:16:32,060 --> 00:16:36,351
Bear in mind that the witness is other
than the accused.

146
00:16:36,351 --> 00:16:41,640
This self, when its fitra — 'he fails who
buries it' (Quran 91:10)...

147
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:50,480
...concealed it and buried it amid
appetites and instincts until it died — yet it is within him, his very self; this same fitra was present at 'Am I not your Lord?

148
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:57,120
They said: Yes' (Quran 7:172).

149
00:16:57,120 --> 00:17:04,120
Now that it has come to this state, this
human who...

150
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:11,120
...is moving upon his animal nature — has
buried his own fitra alive.

151
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:19,920
He has imprisoned his fitra within its own
house; then he himself becomes

152
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:26,061
the wrongdoer. More than fifty times in
the Noble Qur'an God

153
00:17:26,061 --> 00:17:32,304
describes him: ungrateful, a witness
against himself, violent

154
00:17:32,304 --> 00:17:39,161
in love of wealth, a schemer; he develops
problems of belief and of

155
00:17:39,161 --> 00:17:46,121
injustice. 'when kings enter a town they
ruin it and make its mighty

156
00:17:46,121 --> 00:17:52,467
people humbled' (Quran 27:34) is of this
kind. These fifty-odd

157
00:17:52,467 --> 00:17:59,467
censures pertain to the empty half of the
human, for he has buried the

158
00:17:59,467 --> 00:18:06,017
full half. On the Day of Resurrection the
first thing to testify

159
00:18:06,017 --> 00:18:12,670
against the deceived human is 'witnessing
against themselves that

160
00:18:12,670 --> 00:18:19,020
they disbelieved' — this is the very
sentence about the fitra.

161
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:27,095
Some of the great scholars interpreted it
thus: the human

162
00:18:27,095 --> 00:18:34,095
who has taken an animal's form — his whole
being testifies

163
00:18:34,095 --> 00:18:41,095
against himself that he is a plunderer;
this is a practical

164
00:18:41,095 --> 00:18:47,562
testimony. The first witness is the
household witness

165
00:18:47,562 --> 00:18:54,151
('witnessing against themselves'); then it
reaches the

166
00:18:54,151 --> 00:19:00,984
limbs: 'their tongues testify against them
for what they

167
00:19:00,984 --> 00:19:07,695
did' (Quran 24:24). Testimony is other
than confession:

168
00:19:07,695 --> 00:19:14,695
if the criminal speaks, that is
confession; if an outsider

169
00:19:14,695 --> 00:19:20,920
speaks against him, that is testimony. We
are other

170
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:27,920
than our hand, foot, skin and flesh. The
hand that gives or

171
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:34,920
takes bribes over and under the table is a
tool of action.

172
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:42,645
So the hand testifies that this person
took

173
00:19:42,645 --> 00:19:49,370
and gave. The Qur'an does not say the hand

174
00:19:49,370 --> 00:19:56,095
confessed; it says the hand testified — so

175
00:19:56,095 --> 00:20:02,820
the self of the human is the one who gives

176
00:20:02,820 --> 00:20:09,705
and takes; the sin belongs to the human,
to

177
00:20:09,705 --> 00:20:16,705
his empty half, which goes back to
'sounding

178
00:20:16,705 --> 00:20:23,270
clay of molded mire' (Quran 15:26), while

179
00:20:23,270 --> 00:20:29,354
the other half goes back to the divine

180
00:20:29,354 --> 00:20:36,354
in-breathing (nafkh). Testimony may be
external,

181
00:20:36,354 --> 00:20:42,598
or internal — the fitra against nature,

182
00:20:42,598 --> 00:20:49,598
or the limbs against nature. The
nature-bound

183
00:20:49,598 --> 00:20:54,241
human who is 'violent in love

184
00:20:54,241 --> 00:21:01,126
of wealth' must return to 'Say: if you
love

185
00:21:01,126 --> 00:21:08,126
God, follow me, and God will love you'
(Quran

186
00:21:08,126 --> 00:21:13,890
3:31) — the pre-eternal Beloved, who

187
00:21:13,890 --> 00:21:20,780
is God; and God said to His beloved:
Say...

188
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:33,000
Though he can become the beloved of God,
he instead loves these four:

189
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:39,720
branded horses, women and sons, heaped
hoards, and tillage.

190
00:21:40,940 --> 00:21:47,344
It is mineral, plant, animal and human,
and he attaches his heart

191
00:21:47,344 --> 00:21:53,453
to them. After smothering his fitra — 'he
fails who buries it'

192
00:21:53,453 --> 00:21:59,266
(Quran 91:10) — he behaves without
courtesy toward God Most

193
00:21:59,266 --> 00:22:05,276
Holy, becomes ill-mannered and immoral;
and his own faculties

194
00:22:05,276 --> 00:22:11,582
testify against him. This fitra does not
die; it endures, though

195
00:22:11,582 --> 00:22:17,200
imprisoned — 'and to that he is a witness'
(Quran 100:7).

196
00:22:18,320 --> 00:22:24,861
And he loves this wealth intensely. But
the men of God

197
00:22:24,861 --> 00:22:31,402
have surrendered all their wants to God —
giving body,

198
00:22:31,402 --> 00:22:37,822
being cut to pieces, giving their heart's
blood, like

199
00:22:37,822 --> 00:22:44,822
the Master of Martyrs at the Battle of
Uhud (peace be upon

200
00:22:44,822 --> 00:22:51,121
them all). In the inner jihad they chose
the love of

201
00:22:51,121 --> 00:22:58,121
the Beloved over the love of wealth, the
love of the Creator

202
00:22:58,121 --> 00:23:03,693
over the scattered creatures — sons and
women,

203
00:23:03,693 --> 00:23:10,113
heaped hoards, branded horses, tillage —
no; they are

204
00:23:10,113 --> 00:23:16,660
with the love of God. So let us understand
and strive.

205
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:24,976
Let us, as it were, exhume the grave of
the heart — bring out

206
00:23:24,976 --> 00:23:30,868
all its memories, evil deeds, motives,
hypocrisies and

207
00:23:30,868 --> 00:23:37,088
ostentation; and whatever is buried
within, let us revive

208
00:23:37,088 --> 00:23:43,200
it and make it present at the scene of the
Resurrection.

209
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:50,802
The human himself knows that when we
exhume the grave

210
00:23:50,802 --> 00:23:56,302
and what is in the breast comes onto the
table,

211
00:23:56,302 --> 00:24:02,387
he — who was aware — says: 'What is this
record that

212
00:24:02,387 --> 00:24:08,004
leaves nothing small or great but has
enumerated

213
00:24:08,004 --> 00:24:12,920
it?' (Quran 18:49). They can hide nothing.

214
00:24:14,120 --> 00:24:21,120
He is aware now; the inner witness is
present, though he buried it — 'he buried it.'

215
00:24:21,120 --> 00:24:27,887
'What is this record that leaves nothing
small or great but has enumerated it?'

216
00:24:27,887 --> 00:24:34,483
(Quran 18:49) — the great ledgers are with
God and the divine administrators;

217
00:24:34,483 --> 00:24:41,250
but the ordinary register that seems
'forgotten' is not lost: 'a soul will know

218
00:24:41,250 --> 00:24:48,020
what it has brought present' (Quran 81:14)
— the human carries it with himself.

219
00:24:49,060 --> 00:24:56,060
As for what another records — the noble
scribes 'noble writers'

220
00:24:56,060 --> 00:25:02,947
(Quran 82:11) also record it — but 'a soul
will know what

221
00:25:02,947 --> 00:25:09,834
it brought' (Quran 81:14): an indefinite
noun here yields

222
00:25:09,834 --> 00:25:16,834
general meaning, so 'every soul will know
what it has brought

223
00:25:16,834 --> 00:25:23,117
present'; the human himself will make it
present. So

224
00:25:23,117 --> 00:25:30,117
although these verses have been linked to
Hajj and the pilgrim-camels,

225
00:25:30,117 --> 00:25:35,312
the primary reading pertains to the
matters

226
00:25:35,312 --> 00:25:42,312
of jihad; and it makes the human aware
that he has a master of

227
00:25:42,312 --> 00:25:49,080
the house who witnesses his deeds and has
recorded them.

228
00:25:50,800 --> 00:25:57,800
You yourself are the witness — your fitra
is the witness; and you yourself are the criminal

229
00:25:57,800 --> 00:26:03,951
— your animal nature is the criminal. If
witness and witnessed-against are

230
00:26:03,951 --> 00:26:10,951
one, that has meaning only as a practical
testimony — as it were, one turned into a donkey

231
00:26:10,951 --> 00:26:17,185
or a dog — whereas verbal testimonies must
be multiple. This blessed surah,

232
00:26:17,185 --> 00:26:24,001
named al-'Adiyat, is now complete. Many of
its subtleties were laid out in earlier

233
00:26:24,001 --> 00:26:30,734
surahs and verses, and the scholarly
opinions return to these points. We hope God

234
00:26:30,734 --> 00:26:37,734
Most Holy grants the Muslim community a
good understanding of what is the good and welfare

235
00:26:37,734 --> 00:26:44,052
of this world and the next, and that they
know many of these injunctions are

236
00:26:44,052 --> 00:26:51,052
declarative sentences delivered with
performative intent — telling us the best people

237
00:26:51,052 --> 00:26:57,540
of the age are the believers: O believers,
strive to be the best of the world.

238
00:26:57,540 --> 00:27:04,540
And He forgives us and you. Peace be upon
you, and the mercy of God and His blessings.
